  "limits": [
    "Bytes-only and numeric ceilings, PUT-only request use, status restrictions and strict MIME encoding/header budgets are local broker policy; some valid protocol extensions are intentionally denied.",
    "Partial PUT still requires an origin-specific application agreement. Resource length, current validators, authorization and content safety are not inferred.",
    "MCP consumes and validates the entire response before returning it. Go multipart validation retains a bounded content copy and completes at EOF; direct streaming callers must read to EOF and honor errors.",
    "Multipart content is preserved without combining, transfer decoding or caching its parts. Ordinary response bodies keep their streaming behavior.",
    "No new Snort rule or SID. No live routing/deployment verification or proof of universal RFC/W3C conformance, unknown-vulnerability prevention or complete attack coverage."
  ]
